                <pb facs="0504" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/533: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Damm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-06T12:00:00-06:00">April 6,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:43 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From Vice Consul, Ciudad Obregon:</p>
                <p>April 5, 9 p.m. The rebel army retreated from Culiacán to San Bias yesterday
                    where temporary headquarters were established. Seven troop trains carrying
                    approximately 500 troops were used. District <pb facs="0505" n="387"
                        xml:id="pg387"/> through which crossing passes is being looted and forced
                    loans levied irrespective of nationality. Citizens of Los Mochis were compelled
                    to pay 100,000 pesos. Conferred with Commander Comerford of the destroyer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Robert Smith</hi> today making arrangements for the
                    protection of American lives in case of necessity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Damm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
